1
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,839
(This story is entirely fictional)
Let's go get fried chicken.

2
00:00:10,839 --> 00:00:11,279
Coming or not?

3
00:00:11,279 --> 00:00:12,119
No, it's too greasy.

4
00:00:12,119 --> 00:00:13,080
Why?

5
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:14,439
Too greasy.

6
00:00:15,439 --> 00:00:16,839
Yesterday, you promised

7
00:00:16,839 --> 00:00:18,280
to go with me today.

8
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,559
A new squid place opened up.

9
00:00:21,399 --> 00:00:22,280
Let's go eat.

10
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:26,440
(Norwegian Wood by Haruki Murakami)

11
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:32,680
(Based on the novel
Doctor Qin: Executer)

12
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:33,519
You wrote this?

13
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:48,959
(Math problem)

14
00:01:48,959 --> 00:01:50,760
Can't you solve it,
or are you testing me?

15
00:01:51,079 --> 00:01:52,280
I... I can't solve it.

16
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:53,680
I expected your help.

17
00:02:00,159 --> 00:02:01,159
You're okay at taking photos.

18
00:02:01,319 --> 00:02:02,680
Lying isn't your strong suit.

19
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:41,240
=Doctor Qin: Executer=
=Episode 19=

20
00:02:46,479 --> 00:02:47,520
After that day,

21
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:49,240
I understood.

22
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:51,120
All her reckoning

23
00:02:51,599 --> 00:02:52,680
was because

24
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:55,520
she'd suffered pain

25
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,080
I could never imagine.

26
00:03:04,879 --> 00:03:06,680
I don't know how long it was,

27
00:03:09,879 --> 00:03:10,719
but one day,

28
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,240
she came back.

29
00:03:24,879 --> 00:03:26,080
It's all over.

30
00:03:29,439 --> 00:03:32,120
Today is the anniversary
of my dad's death.

31
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:36,120
He jumped from a building.

32
00:03:43,439 --> 00:03:45,039
I did one wrong thing.

33
00:03:46,199 --> 00:03:47,439
To cover it up,

34
00:03:49,199 --> 00:03:51,159
I did more wrong things.

35
00:03:51,879 --> 00:03:55,719
Then I did many, many even worse things

36
00:03:56,599 --> 00:03:58,520
to cover it up.

37
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:08,759
Tell me,

38
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:10,879
am I even worse

39
00:04:12,639 --> 00:04:14,759
than the people

40
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:16,720
I killed?

41
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,680
Why am I telling you all this?

42
00:04:28,879 --> 00:04:30,680
I know you've been painting me.

43
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,959
Why do you paint me?

44
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:36,600
Because...

45
00:04:39,959 --> 00:04:41,839
you're beautiful.

46
00:04:44,839 --> 00:04:45,639
Your...

47
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,160
eyes...

48
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:51,120
hold stories.

49
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:56,279
Am I pretty?

50
00:04:59,879 --> 00:05:01,879
I don't remember what I look like.

51
00:05:03,879 --> 00:05:05,120
For these twenty-some years,

52
00:05:06,079 --> 00:05:08,319
I've never really looked at myself.

53
00:05:09,519 --> 00:05:10,639
Only two guys

54
00:05:12,439 --> 00:05:14,120
once took photos of me.

55
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:19,160
It was in a field of sunflowers.

56
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:54,720
Can you paint another portrait of me?

57
00:06:11,959 --> 00:06:13,519
A portrait with eyes.

58
00:06:14,519 --> 00:06:15,519
And a smile.

59
00:06:16,879 --> 00:06:17,720
Is that okay?

60
00:06:57,959 --> 00:06:59,079
Let's stop here.

61
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:12,360
She told me

62
00:07:14,279 --> 00:07:15,519
she didn't want to kill me.

63
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:17,560
I didn't do anything wrong.

64
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:20,879
But I saw everything

65
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:22,319
and painted it.

66
00:07:22,839 --> 00:07:24,160
So I have to die.

67
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:32,600
Ms. Zhang?

68
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:33,879
Ms. Zhang, what's wrong?

69
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:34,920
Zhang Lanfen?

70
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:36,040
Zhang Lanfen?

71
00:07:36,279 --> 00:07:37,279
You're safe now.

72
00:07:37,279 --> 00:07:38,120
Tell me,

73
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:39,480
where is she now?

74
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:40,600
She...

75
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:44,720
She's dead!

76
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:45,839
Dead?

77
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:47,079
How did she die?

78
00:07:47,079 --> 00:07:48,079
Where's the body?

79
00:07:49,160 --> 00:07:49,959
Zhang Lanfen?

80
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:51,519
Zhang Lanfen?

81
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:52,399
Dead...

82
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,360
Go get a doctor!

83
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:54,000
Got it!

84
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:55,560
They're all dead!

85
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:56,120
Zhang Lanfen?

86
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:56,879
Zhang Lanfen?

87
00:07:57,519 --> 00:07:58,160
Zhang Lanfen?

88
00:07:58,160 --> 00:07:59,360
All dead...

89
00:08:01,279 --> 00:08:02,120
(Qin,)

90
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:03,879
(Zhang Lanfen says
Jin Keke is already dead.)

91
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:05,720
(Qin, did you hear that?)

92
00:08:06,759 --> 00:08:07,560
Impossible.

93
00:08:09,759 --> 00:08:11,120
Where's the body? How did she die?

94
00:08:11,759 --> 00:08:13,160
(Zhang Lanfen is extremely emotional.)

95
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:14,120
(She won't say anything.)

96
00:08:14,199 --> 00:08:15,199
(We suspect that...)

97
00:08:15,199 --> 00:08:16,279
You suspect

98
00:08:17,279 --> 00:08:18,879
Zhang Lanfen killed her?

99
00:08:18,879 --> 00:08:19,480
(Dr. Qin,)

100
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:22,160
(we found blood spots
on Zhang Lanfen's clothes.)

101
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:24,160
(DNA test says it's Jin Keke's.)

102
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:32,720
All dead!

103
00:08:32,799 --> 00:08:33,600
All dead...

104
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:34,519
Zhang Lanfen?

105
00:08:34,559 --> 00:08:36,120
All dead...

106
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:36,840
Zhang Lanfen?

107
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:37,520
(Want to save her? Come alone
to the abandoned water plant!)

108
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:38,840
(Remember, you're not a cop for now!)

109
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:40,160
(If you call the police,
you'll never see your lost love again!)

110
00:09:55,919 --> 00:09:56,720
Dead?

111
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:58,039
Where's the body?

112
00:10:07,679 --> 00:10:09,279
We have to get Zhang Lanfen to talk.

113
00:10:09,279 --> 00:10:10,720
We suspect she killed Jin Keke.

114
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:12,240
She fakes illness to stall for time.

115
00:10:14,159 --> 00:10:14,960
Chief.

116
00:10:17,159 --> 00:10:18,840
There's rust
in Zhang Lanfen's fingernails.

117
00:10:18,879 --> 00:10:20,159
Sunflower pollen in her hair.

118
00:10:20,159 --> 00:10:21,360
Different cat hairs on her clothes.

119
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:26,039
Rust.

120
00:10:26,399 --> 00:10:27,200
Pollen.

121
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:28,279
Cat hair.

122
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:29,200
Zhang Lanfen was held

123
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:30,360
in Su Shi's cat shelter!

124
00:10:34,559 --> 00:10:35,519
What are you waiting for?

125
00:10:35,559 --> 00:10:36,440
Get moving!

126
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:37,080
Yes, sir!

127
00:10:43,920 --> 00:10:45,440
(Police)

128
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:48,720
(FAN A8028 Police)

129
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:51,160
(Police)

130
00:10:56,159 --> 00:10:57,120
Move in!

131
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,279
Mr. Han, no one here!

132
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:24,799
No one here!

133
00:11:25,159 --> 00:11:26,320
Report: no one here!

134
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:35,000
(Liang, we've got something.)

135
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,759
(Song Yalan talked to Jin Keke.)

136
00:11:36,759 --> 00:11:38,080
Let's go! Song Yalan's place!

137
00:12:02,399 --> 00:12:04,559
(Mom, I miss you.)

138
00:12:06,279 --> 00:12:07,559
(How have you been?)

139
00:12:07,679 --> 00:12:08,480
(Keke,)

140
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:11,279
(are you doing something dangerous?)

141
00:12:11,399 --> 00:12:12,799
(The police visited our house.)

142
00:12:12,799 --> 00:12:13,759
(Are you okay?)

143
00:12:13,759 --> 00:12:15,559
(I can't come back for a while.)

144
00:12:16,879 --> 00:12:18,639
(Can you bring me some clothes?)

145
00:12:19,679 --> 00:12:21,840
(Mom, I miss you.)

146
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:25,000
(No power strips or chargers on the bed)
(How have you been?)

147
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:25,919
(Turn off water after washing veggies)
(Keke,)

148
00:12:26,399 --> 00:12:28,720
(are you doing something dangerous?)

149
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:30,240
(The police visited our house.)

150
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:31,200
(Are you okay?)

151
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:33,000
(I can't come back for a while.)

152
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:33,600
(Zhang Xiaodong)

153
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:36,080
(Can you bring me some clothes?)

154
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:39,360
(If anything happens, contact Keke)
(Mom, I miss you.)

155
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:41,159
(Le Tianyi)

156
00:12:41,159 --> 00:12:42,600
(How have you been?)

157
00:12:42,639 --> 00:12:43,440
(Keke,)

158
00:12:43,919 --> 00:12:46,240
(are you doing something dangerous?)

159
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:47,720
(The police visited our house.)

160
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:51,159
Remote control?

161
00:12:57,720 --> 00:12:58,519
Han Liang.

162
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:00,159
Jin Keke is at the water plant
in Hailun District.

163
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:00,960
She's in danger.

164
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:01,840
Call for backup!

165
00:13:07,519 --> 00:13:08,279
What's wrong?

166
00:13:09,879 --> 00:13:11,360
Qin Ming says Jin Keke is in danger.

167
00:13:12,399 --> 00:13:13,919
Isn't Jin Keke dead?

168
00:13:14,279 --> 00:13:15,519
Qin Ming called?

169
00:13:15,639 --> 00:13:17,080
It really was Qin Ming.

170
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:22,520
(FAN A 95T79)

171
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:32,240
Keke?

172
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:33,279
Keke?

173
00:13:33,519 --> 00:13:35,840
(Qin Ming, you're finally here.)

174
00:13:36,759 --> 00:13:38,279
(Did you find the Executer?)

175
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:40,799
(Do you know the truth?)

176
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:44,120
(Or is it just
your self-righteous truth?)

177
00:13:45,399 --> 00:13:48,200
(Today you'll find
the answer to the puzzle.)

178
00:13:48,919 --> 00:13:49,840
(However,)

179
00:13:50,279 --> 00:13:52,120
(you'll also have to pay the price.)

180
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:53,519
(Are you ready?)

181
00:13:54,519 --> 00:13:57,519
(Welcome to the Executer's judgment.)

182
00:13:59,519 --> 00:14:00,320
(Qin Ming!)

183
00:14:02,039 --> 00:14:02,840
(Qin Ming!)

184
00:14:05,519 --> 00:14:06,320
Keke?

185
00:14:08,879 --> 00:14:09,679
Keke?

186
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:13,000
(Qin Ming!)

187
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:14,120
Keke?

188
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:22,279
Keke?

189
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:25,919
Qin Ming!

190
00:14:26,399 --> 00:14:28,080
It's dangerous here! Go now!

191
00:14:28,679 --> 00:14:29,639
Go!

192
00:14:30,519 --> 00:14:33,120
Don't come any closer! Go now!

193
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:37,879
Keke!

194
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:57,840
Qin Ming!

195
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:16,919
Keke!

196
00:15:17,279 --> 00:15:18,080
(Qin Ming,)

197
00:15:18,559 --> 00:15:21,440
(beneath Jin Keke's feet
is a current leading to hell.)

198
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:25,879
(The voltage in the current
won't kill her right away.)

199
00:15:26,679 --> 00:15:29,200
(Countless currents will pass
through her pores,)

200
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:31,120
(boring into every nerve in her body.)

201
00:15:32,799 --> 00:15:35,919
(She'll endure the most extreme pain,)

202
00:15:36,759 --> 00:15:40,600
(then slowly die in agony.)

203
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:41,919
Who are you?

204
00:15:42,679 --> 00:15:43,799
Who on earth are you?

205
00:15:43,799 --> 00:15:45,080
(Never mind who I am.)

206
00:15:45,679 --> 00:15:47,279
(Jin Keke killed so many people.)

207
00:15:48,519 --> 00:15:51,039
(She deserves a taste
of being killed herself.)

208
00:15:51,279 --> 00:15:52,080
(Qin Ming,)

209
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:55,279
(see the gun hanging beside you?)

210
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:59,320
(You should know what it's for.)

211
00:15:59,879 --> 00:16:01,600
(I suggest you decide quickly.)

212
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:05,360
(Either watch her be tortured to death,)

213
00:16:05,919 --> 00:16:07,519
(or give her a quick death.)

214
00:16:08,519 --> 00:16:09,960
(I'm waiting for your choice.)

215
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:14,039
(Qin Ming,)

216
00:16:14,399 --> 00:16:16,279
(you were top three in marksmanship
at the police academy.)

217
00:16:17,279 --> 00:16:19,080
(So I only gave you one bullet.)

218
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:20,559
(Shoot accurately.)

219
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:22,639
(Otherwise,)

220
00:16:23,159 --> 00:16:24,679
(she'll suffer even more.)

221
00:16:30,159 --> 00:16:30,960
Qin Ming!

222
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:48,519
Qin Ming,

223
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:51,240
I died ten years ago.

224
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:54,720
You still have a future.

225
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:57,559
Don't throw yourself away!

226
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:05,720
I'm sorry, Keke.

227
00:17:08,079 --> 00:17:09,720
I won't let you hurt anymore.

228
00:18:03,519 --> 00:18:04,319
Keke!

229
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:06,119
(You actually fired.)

230
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:07,920
(It was a blank.)

231
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:10,359
(Surprised? Unexpected?)

232
00:18:11,440 --> 00:18:13,400
(Qin Ming, good performance.)

233
00:18:14,839 --> 00:18:15,640
(However,)

234
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:18,039
(I can see you don't want her to die.)

235
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:20,440
(Then let's play another round.)

236
00:18:21,519 --> 00:18:22,319
(Next,)

237
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:24,079
(we play for real.)

238
00:18:26,839 --> 00:18:27,640
Keke!

239
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:30,720
Qin Ming!

240
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:31,759
(Qin Ming,)

241
00:18:32,359 --> 00:18:33,720
(are you willing to trade your life...)

242
00:18:33,839 --> 00:18:34,519
No!

243
00:18:34,519 --> 00:18:36,039
(for Jin Keke's life?)

244
00:18:36,759 --> 00:18:39,359
(You have five seconds to decide.)

245
00:18:45,519 --> 00:18:46,319
Qin Ming!

246
00:18:46,519 --> 00:18:47,319
Keke...

247
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:50,920
In the first letter I wrote you,

248
00:18:51,559 --> 00:18:52,839
the answer to that problem

249
00:18:53,559 --> 00:18:55,079
was my message to you.

250
00:18:57,280 --> 00:18:57,560
(Given the perimeter of △PF₁F₂ is 10,)

251
00:18:57,561 --> 00:18:58,440
(with fixed points F₁(–c,0), F₂(c,0),
and point P(x,y) where |PF₁|+|PF₂|=10,)

252
00:18:58,440 --> 00:18:59,600
(Find P's path equation c.
If c is tangent to y=x+b, find b.)

253
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:02,000
(|PF₁|...)

254
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:07,560
♪Wind through blooms, waves of gold♪

255
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:11,560
♪Chalk dust falls on white uniforms♪

256
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:17,320
♪You turned and took the summer away♪

257
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:19,640
Qin Ming!

258
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:25,560
♪Leaving an unsolved ellipse equation♪

259
00:19:28,480 --> 00:19:32,710
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

260
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:37,580
♪Milk tea cools on the stone steps♪

261
00:19:37,580 --> 00:19:41,580
♪Sea wind tugs at your sleeve♪

262
00:19:42,070 --> 00:19:45,930
♪Unspoken words just flee and fade♪

263
00:19:54,910 --> 00:19:58,820
♪The marks on the desk
have faded yellow♪

264
00:19:58,820 --> 00:20:01,800
♪I turned around,
and a gunshot rang out♪

265
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:05,940
♪No one can truly feel another's pain♪

266
00:20:05,940 --> 00:20:10,170
♪The wind is cold,
a fading shadow sways♪

267
00:20:10,170 --> 00:20:14,890
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

268
00:20:14,890 --> 00:20:19,040
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

269
00:20:19,910 --> 00:20:23,690
♪A bullet pierces the spring night♪

270
00:20:23,690 --> 00:20:27,780
♪You sink into the vast crowd♪

271
00:20:36,740 --> 00:20:40,950
♪Years later, when we meet again♪

272
00:20:40,950 --> 00:20:45,290
♪Don't mention this moonlit night♪

273
00:20:45,290 --> 00:20:49,060
♪The waves smooth
two lines of footprints♪

274
00:20:49,060 --> 00:20:51,960
♪Half a cup of sweetness
sinks into the sand♪

275
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:56,750
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

276
00:20:56,750 --> 00:21:01,400
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

277
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:03,660
♪Wind back to shore,
clouds back to hills♪

278
00:21:03,660 --> 00:21:05,800
♪We stop here in this night♪

279
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:10,220
♪This is the past, the only,
the last look back♪

280
00:21:10,220 --> 00:21:16,200
